;\n+\tif (solver_priority == p_priority) {\n+\t\treturn;\n+\t}\n+\n+\tsolver_priority = MAX(0, p_priority);","path":"modules/jolt_physics/joints/jolt_joint_3d.cpp","commit_id":"c52897bec21a2559a25a46acee6e8063d120b89f","original_commit_id":"c52897bec21a2559a25a46acee6e8063d120b89f","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thinking about it again, I don't think even a warning is needed. The documentation about this parameter has been wrong for a while, and the inspector restricts it to positive, non-zero values. I think warnings are nice when scripting, but documentation and the inspector rejecting negative input is enough here. I think if someone considers using a negative value, they would first ask \"Can I use a negative, and what would that mean?\" and see the inspector prevents the input and the documentation saying negatives not allowed and will be quietly clamped with `MAX(0, priority)`\r\n","created_at":"2026-06-19T15:16:26Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T15:16:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119976#discussion_r3443327866","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine